msgid "To verify them, resolve that {code0} against the GDHCN trust list rather than against any copy of the certificate shipped beside the QR code. The DID trust list endpoints for the development, user-acceptance testing and production environments are listed under <a0>Trustlist Distribution Endpoints</a0>; this example is issued in DEV, so its Document Signing Certificate is on the DEV trust list. Fetching the signing certificate from the trust list is the verification path the specification defines, and the only one that tells a verifier the key is still trusted — a certificate distributed alongside the certificate it signed proves nothing about that."
